actor makes the risk more likely or severe, else \"negative\" (used only for \"drives\"); \"affects_id\": the id of the goal or an outcome the risk would hurt; \"direction\": \"negative\" when the risk lowers it, \"positive\" when it raises it; \"relies_on\": what the option relies on, 12 words or fewer, starting with a verb or noun (e.g. \"filling both roles quickly\"); \"watch_for\": the early sign, 8 words or fewer}.\nA \"relies_on\" risk must name one option: shared preconditions cannot be applied yet and will be refused. It stays on the model with no links and is left out of the Run until the model can apply it to that option alone.\nThe goal: {\"id\":\"weekly_support_capacity\",\"label\":\"Weekly support capacity\"}.\nGoal and outcomes (affects_id): [{\"id\":\"weekly_support_capacity\",\"label\":\"Weekly support capacity\"},{\"id\":\"additional_specialist_capacity\",\"label\":\"Additional specialist capacity\"}].\nThe user's options and the factors each one changes: [{\"id\":\"add_one_specialist\",\"label\":\"Add one specialist\",\"changes\":[{\"id\":\"additional_specialists\",\"label\":\"Additional specialists\"}]},{\"id\":\"add_part_time_specialist\",\"label\":\"Add part-time specialist\",\"changes\":[{\"id\":\"additional_specialists\",\"label\":\"Additional specialists\"}]}].\nAt least one item must hit the option the brief proposes, {\"id\":\"add_one_specialist\",\"label\":\"Add one specialist\"}: a way it could fall short.\nAll factors: [{\"id\":\"existing_team_capacity\",\"label\":\"Existing team capacity\"},{\"id\":\"additional_specialists\",\"label\":\"Additional specialists\"},{\"id\":\"tickets_resolved_per_specialist_per_week\",\"label\":\"Tickets resolved per specialist per week\"}].\nRisks already in the model (never suggest these again): [\"Specialist productivity variability\"].\nUse only these ids. Never write a probability, percentage, figure, likely, chance, best, recommend, winner, leads or ahead.",
